%I A402457 #14 Nov 22 2026 10:00:04
%S A402457 2,3,5,13,19,23,31,37,47,271,313,499,4567,8731,8933,11789,14401,33893
%N A402457 Primes p such that 3*p# - 1 is prime, where prime(n)# = A002110(n).
%C A402457 Primes prime(n) such that A402506(n) is prime.
%C A402457 a(19) > 10^5. - _Michael S. Branicky_, Nov 21 2026
%e A402457 3*2-1 = 5 is prime, so 2 is a term;
%e A402457 3*2*3-1 = 17 is prime, so 3 is a term;
%e A402457 3*2*3*5-1 = 89 is prime, so 5 is a term;
%e A402457 3*2*3*5*7-1 = 629 = 17*37, so 7 is not a term;
%e A402457 3*2*3*5*7*11-1 = 6929 = 13^2*41, so 11 is not a term;
%e A402457 3*2*3*5*7*11*13-1 = 90089 is prime, so 13 is a term;
%e A402457 3*2*3*5*7*11*13*17-1 = 1531529 = 1109*1381, so 17 is not a term;
%e A402457 3*2*3*5*7*11*13*17*19-1 = 29099069 is prime, so 19 is a term.
%o A402457 (PARI) my(P=3); forprime(p=2, 1000, P*=p; if(ispseudoprime(P-1), print1(p, ", ")))
%Y A402457 Cf. A002110 (primorials), A402506.
%Y A402457 See A402499 for a list of related sequences.
%K A402457 nonn,more,new
%O A402457 1,1
%A A402457 _Jianing Song_, Nov 19 2026
